1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Now a real run.

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:05,000
In Jenkins I choose Build with Parameters.

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:25,000
The form shows the three parameters of the Jenkinsfile with their defaults: APP ENV staging, so it deploys to the staging environment on port eight thousand eighty one; BRANCH develop, the integration branch; and REGISTRY localhost colon five thousand, the local registry.

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,000
I click Build.

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:31,000
This is the stage view of the new build, filling in live.

6
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Stage one, checkout, fetches the commit and builds the version and commit tag.

7
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Stage two installs the dependencies in a fresh virtual environment.

8
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Stage three, static checks, compiles the code and runs the linter.

9
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Stage four runs the unit and integration tests.

10
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,000
If any of these turns red, everything after it is skipped.

11
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Stage five runs the Selenium browser tests in headless Chromium, about twenty seconds.

12
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Stage six packages the source archive and writes its checksum.

13
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Stage seven builds the two Docker images, the application and Nginx, tagged with the version and the commit.

14
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Stage eight publishes both images to the local registry.

15
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:19,000
Only code that passed every test gets this far.

16
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Stage nine deploys: Docker compose pulls the published images and starts the containers, and waits until they are healthy.

17
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Stage ten, the health check, asks the running application for its version and commit and compares them with this build.

18
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:43,000
When the whole row is green, the build is a success.

19
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,000
I wait for the build to finish.

20
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:50,000
The console of the new build confirms each step.

21
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Docker build created the application image, tagged with the registry, the version and the commit.

22
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Docker push published it.

23
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Docker compose up with the wait option started the containers, and Docker reported them healthy.

24
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Finally the pipeline printed deployed, with the version, commit tag and the staging address.

25
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:16,000
Every deployment writes a record, archived with the build.

26
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:26,000
It says the environment, the branch, the version, the commit, the image tag, the names of both images, the address, and the Jenkins build address.

27
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:33,000
This is the traceability: from a running staging container back to one commit and one build.


